From: Joshua Bryan <45343084+rafe-walker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 13:24:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] fix(plugin-mcp): pass the reason of a validation
 refusal through (research v2.2)

Research v1 set isError on a refused create or update, but the text kept only
Payload's headline, "The following field is invalid: Priority", which names
the field and drops the reason REST gives. The reasons are in the
ValidationError's data.errors; create, update and delete now append them:

  The following field is invalid: Priority (priority: 9 is greater than the
  max allowed Value of 5.)

isError is unchanged. A bulk update still reports each document's headline
only: Payload's bulk operation keeps only error.message per document.

Tests: refusalReason.spec.ts (3).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
